## Why This Is Asked
This problem introduces a dynamic programming angle where subarrays are weighted by their block index. It tests the ability to transform interval sums into prefix sums, derive a two-dimensional DP over position and block count, and implement solution reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums for O(1) interval sum computation
- 2D DP over position and block count
- Solution reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time complexity: O(n²k); Space complexity: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxScorePartition(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const P = [0];
  for (let x of A) P.push(P[P.length-1] + x);
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    dp[i][1] = P[i];
  }

  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let p = t-1; p < i; p++) {
        const score = dp[p][t-1] + (P[i] - P[p]) * t;
        if (score > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = score;
          parent[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct partitions
  const partitions = [];
  let end = n;
  for (let t = k; t >= 1; t--) {
    const start = parent[end][t];
    partitions.unshift([start+1, end]);
    end = start;
  }

  return { maxScore: dp[n][k], partitions };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to transform per-element cost into a standard max-sum DP for exactly k non-overlapping subarrays and to reconstruct endpoints. It emphasizes exact-k and non-overlap constraints common in analytics problems.

## Key Concepts
- Transform to B[i] = A[i] - c and reduce to max-sum of k non-overlapping subarrays
- DP states: local[i][t] for subarray ending at i; glob[i][t] for best so far with t subarrays
- Recurrences and reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(B, k) {
  const n = B.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const local = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const glob  = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  local[0][0] = 0; glob[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      local[i][t] = Math.max(local[i-1][t] + B[i-1], glob[i-1][t-1] + B[i-1]);
      glob[i][t] = Math.max(glob[i-1][t], local[i][t]);
    }
  }
  return {max: glob[n][k], endpoints: []};
}
```

